                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_300">Leicester,
                                Leicestershire, Collegiate church of the Annunciation of St Mary the
                                Virgin, in the Newarke</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card records the following context for the rejection:
                                Cf. C. Wordsworth and H. Littlehales, <title>Old Service-Books of
                                    the English Church</title>, pp. 140-41: 'belonged to the chantry
                                founded by W. Wyggeston (c. 1513) in connexion with the Collegiate
                                Church of St. Marys, Leicester "in the Newark"' - this may apply to
                                all the Wyggeston manuscripts and printed books, but there is no
                                real evidence that they belonged to the chantry. One of them (MS 11)
                                was bequeathed to St. Marys in 1537.</p></provenance>
                    </history>
